ROCR-Runtime: issue _mm_sfence() in SdmaQueue::RingDoorbell before the
doorbell store, the same fence that AqlQueue::StoreRelaxed issues before its
own doorbell store.

WHY
---
SdmaQueue::RingDoorbell publishes a submission with a release store to the
write pointer, a release thread fence, and the doorbell store. On x86 a
release fence orders ordinary write-back stores but not write-combining
stores. The AQL doorbell path fences with _mm_sfence(), so it does not
depend on the memory type of the ring. The SDMA path has no such fence.

On gfx803 the ring is write-back memory. amdgpu sets no
AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_CPU_GTT_USWC on the KFD path (amdgpu_amdkfd_gpuvm.c uses
alloc_flags = 0 for GTT), and gmc_v8 ignores AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_UNCACHED.
x86 store order then already puts the packet stores ahead of the doorbell,
so this fence changes no result on this card. The patch stays because it
costs one instruction per SDMA submission and keeps the two doorbell paths
identical.

An intermittent hang in SDMA-routed copies on gfx803 is not this bug. That
hang comes from VRAM clocked above its rating. See "Required host setup"
in README.md.

WHAT
----
- amd_sdma_queue.cpp: _mm_sfence() between the release thread fence and the
  doorbell store in SdmaQueue::RingDoorbell.

Applies to: rocm-systems release/therock-10.1, commit
7da43026e4f2ef7600433c38c820732f7a205d22. The change is not gated on the
architecture, so it affects every SDMA queue.

NOT YET RE-VERIFIED ON REAL HARDWARE against this commit.

diff --git a/projects/rocr-runtime/runtime/hsa-runtime/core/runtime/amd_sdma_queue.cpp b/projects/rocr-runtime/runtime/hsa-runtime/core/runtime/amd_sdma_queue.cpp
index 91a0804..b2ea694 100644
--- a/projects/rocr-runtime/runtime/hsa-runtime/core/runtime/amd_sdma_queue.cpp
+++ b/projects/rocr-runtime/runtime/hsa-runtime/core/runtime/amd_sdma_queue.cpp
@@ -239,6 +239,10 @@ hsa_status_t SdmaQueue::RingDoorbell(uint64_t write_index) {
   // canonical write pointer and packet stores are visible before the doorbell.
   atomic::Store(queue_wptr_, write_index, std::memory_order_release);
   std::atomic_thread_fence(std::memory_order_release);
+  // Same fence as AqlQueue::StoreRelaxed issues before its doorbell write, so
+  // that the doorbell never depends on the ring being mapped write-back for the
+  // packet stores to reach memory first.
+  _mm_sfence();
   *queue_doorbell_ = write_index;
 
   if (core::Runtime::runtime_singleton_->thunkLoader()->IsDXG() ||
